    "answer": {
      "short": "$2\\leq x\\leq3$.",
      "worked": "Since $x^2+1>0$ for all real $x$, multiply both sides by $5(x^2+1)>0$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}5(x-1)&\\geq x^2+1\\\\x^2-5x+6&\\leq0\\\\(x-2)(x-3)&\\leq0\\\\2\\leq x&\\leq3\\end{align*}$$",
